# Later rules win in gitattributes, so the general case goes first and the
# exceptions follow. (Learned the hard way: with these two blocks the other way
# round, `* text=auto` silently overrode the -text below and the CSVs still
# arrived with CRLF.)
* text=auto

# The provided files must arrive byte-identical on every machine.
#
# Git's default on Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout. That leaves the content
# unchanged but the BYTES different, which breaks two things: the sha256 values
# analysis/findings.json records for provenance, and the exercise's instruction that
# the provided data is not to be modified. -text switches the conversion off, so what
# we were given is what every reviewer gets.
data/*.csv -text
model/*.pkl -text binary
